# State management

UI state is a `Bloc` with freezed events and states. Register it with `@Injectable()`.

```dart
@Injectable()
class NewsBloc extends Bloc<NewsEvent, NewsState> {
  NewsBloc(this._loadNewsUC) : super(const NewsState.initial()) {
    on<_NewsLoadEvent>(_loadNews);
  }

  void init(String source) => add(NewsEvent.load(source));
}
```

```dart
@freezed
sealed class NewsState with _$NewsState {
  const factory NewsState.initial() = NewsInitialState;
  const factory NewsState.loading() = NewsLoadingState;
  const factory NewsState.loaded(NewsViewModel viewModel) = NewsLoadedState;
}
```

Pages create the bloc and branch with `state.when`:

```dart
BlocProvider(
  create: (context) => get<NewsBloc>()..init(widget.source),
  child: BlocBuilder<NewsBloc, NewsState>(
    builder: (context, state) => state.when(
      initial: () => const SizedBox(),
      loading: () => const Center(child: CircularProgressIndicator()),
      loaded: (uiModel) => NewsContent(model: uiModel),
    ),
  ),
)
```

- Events and states are `part of` the bloc file.
- Map domain models to `view/model` types before they reach `loaded`.
- Cancel `StreamSubscription`s in `close()`.
- `FavoritesBloc` is provided above the router in `App` because more than one tab reads it. Feature-local blocs stay on the page.
- Widget-local controllers (`TabController`, text fields) stay on the `State` that owns them.
